Pair the background image label with its combo box

The popup menu page holds the label of the background image in form
row 8, beside the combo box for the gradient orientation. The image
combo box sits in row 9, and row 9 carries no label. QFormLayout pairs
the label role and the field role of one row, so the page names the
wrong control. The tooltip of that combo box states the gradient
orientation, and the label beside it contradicts the tooltip.

Move the label to row 9. The background page already holds the wanted
shape. Its gradient combo box takes a row of its own, and the image
label stands beside the image combo box.

The change sits on the branch work/dialog-state of the local tree, as commit 11 of 12.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfigbase.ui b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfigbase.ui
index 5d818332..04b623d1 100644
--- a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfigbase.ui
+++ b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfigbase.ui
@@ -3283,7 +3283,7 @@
          </property>
         </widget>
        </item>
-       <item row="8" column="0">
+       <item row="9" column="0">
         <widget class="QLabel" name="label_xx">
          <property name="text">
           <string>Background image:</string>
